# colab/VERSION -- the notebook's revision, and the ONE PLACE it is declared.
#
# The first line is the version. Everything below is a log.
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT JUST A NUMBER IN THE NOTEBOOK. The notebook you are
# running lives in your BROWSER, and the repository is what `git reset
# --hard' updates. Those two are different copies and they have already
# disagreed: the package list was corrected upstream, the cell in the
# browser stayed as it was, and the same run failed twice for the same
# reason with a corrected fix sitting on disk the whole time.
#
# So the number is declared HERE, the notebook carries the number it was
# published at, and section 1 compares them and says so. A version you
# can read is worth something; a version that CHECKS ITSELF against the
# repository is worth the thing that actually went wrong.
#
# Bump this whenever a notebook CELL changes. A change to prereqs.sh,
# preflight.sh or build.sh does not need a bump -- those come from the
# repository already, which is the point of their being scripts.
